{"lines":[{"w":0.016460905075073251,"t":"E","x":0.088477366289623868,"c":1,"y":0.38517441888522563,"h":0.013081394460653373},{"y":0.64534883698273704,"h":0.013081395583944611,"x":0.088477366289623882,"c":1,"t":"F","w":0.016460905075073251},{"x":0.79166500803877693,"y":0.097773287340302995,"w":0.079276053110758582,"h":0.016083906059130348,"c":1,"t":"Reading"},{"t":"This complicated process and questionable outcome begs the question: what is","h":0.01598837238037687,"x":0.12962962387285151,"y":0.14244186031901696,"w":0.70370371500651041,"c":1},{"y":0.15842167277484875,"h":0.01599693129846147,"t":"the actual point of this technology? 'For us, the goal has always been replacing","w":0.69958847045898442,"c":1,"x":0.12962963230137206},{"h":0.016195524146054296,"c":1,"t":"the extinct species with a suitable replacement,' explains Novak. When it comes","x":0.12962963118087903,"y":0.17579505306368359,"w":0.71193415323893228},{"w":0.69958847045898431,"h":0.016195524146054185,"x":0.12962963297669811,"t":"to breeding, band-tailed pigeons scatter and make maybe one or two nests per","y":0.19316843320034605,"c":1},{"w":0.69547322591145833,"c":1,"y":0.20930232542206151,"h":0.017441860778592999,"x":0.12962964208542302,"t":"hectare, whereas passenger pigeons were very social and would make 10,000"},{"h":0.018455396973483085,"y":0.22432184488937468,"c":1,"x":0.13160940207872027,"t":"or more nests in one hectare.' Since the disappearance of this key species,","w":0.66479253133138017},{"t":"ecosystems in the eastern US have suffered, as the lack of disturbance caused","y":0.24263839809876742,"c":1,"w":0.69753087361653643,"x":0.13168723804019122,"h":0.016195524146054185},{"w":0.69341562906901044,"h":0.016032884483202503,"t":"by thousands of passenger pigeons wrecking trees and branches means there","c":1,"x":0.13168724708554369,"y":0.26017441845847622},{"c":1,"t":"has been minimal need for regrowth. This has left forests stagnant and therefore","y":0.27616279055049131,"w":0.70781890869140629,"x":0.13168725341095702,"h":0.01598837238037687},{"t":"unwelcoming to the plants and animals which evolved to help regenerate the forest","h":0.016012340046912987,"c":1,"y":0.29358068335002374,"x":0.13168723234837215,"w":0.73456792195638032},{"w":0.71810699462890626,"c":1,"x":0.13168724332217116,"y":0.30948174313349497,"t":"after a disturbance. According to Novak, a hybridised band-tailed pigeon, with the","h":0.016195524146054185},{"c":1,"t":"added nesting habits of a passenger pigeon, could, in theory, re-establish that","x":0.13168723076662056,"h":0.016015764400450827,"y":0.3270348835748087,"w":0.68930043538411456},{"x":0.12955422967044114,"y":0.34030042488659573,"t":"forest disturbance, thereby creating a habitat necessary for a great many other","w":0.69769505818684896,"c":1,"h":0.020691380764766842},{"t":"native species to thrive.","y":0.36042402837598575,"w":0.2139917755126953,"c":1,"x":0.13168723970888133,"h":0.016029460129664774},{"x":0.13163006618743339,"y":0.3849372722882336,"w":0.68941838582356763,"c":1,"t":"Another popular candidate for this technology is the woolly mammoth. George","h":0.018658029176601865},{"c":1,"w":0.71399175008138027,"t":"Church, professor at Harvard Medical School and leader of the Woolly Mammoth","y":0.40253239096760574,"x":0.13168725242844573,"h":0.016195524146054296},{"h":0.017496644818740803,"x":0.13374485742868331,"c":1,"y":0.4186046510033854,"w":0.71193415323893228,"t":"Revival Project, has been focusing on cold resistance, the main way in which the"},{"h":0.015988372380376759,"t":"extinct woolly mammoth and its nearest living relative, the Asian elephant, differ.","w":0.70781890869140629,"x":0.13168725337034629,"c":1,"y":0.43604651148174756},{"x":0.13168723610033756,"w":0.70987655639648439,"t":"By pinpointing which genetic traits made it possible for mammoths to survive the","y":0.45347467623103732,"h":0.014548579711374909,"c":1},{"h":0.017667844522968212,"w":0.72839508056640634,"t":"icy climate of the tundra, the project's goal is to return mammoths, or a mammoth-","c":1,"x":0.1296296201243598,"y":0.46937573598739168},{"y":0.48417611126676119,"h":0.019022542820942845,"c":1,"w":0.71823867797851559,"x":0.13163010931903671,"t":"like species, to the area. 'My highest priority would be preserving the endangered"},{"y":0.50145348820252977,"w":0.73045267740885422,"c":1,"h":0.017441860778592999,"t":"Asian elephant,' says Church, 'expanding their range to the huge ecosystem of the","x":0.13168724120812442},{"h":0.016019188192342826,"t":"tundra. Necessary adaptations would include smaller ears, thicker hair, and extra","x":0.13168725243066851,"y":0.5203180212511922,"c":1,"w":0.71399175008138027},{"t":"insulating fat, all for the purpose of reducing heat loss in the tundra, and all traits","x":0.12962963110317824,"y":0.53621908103441507,"w":0.71193415323893228,"c":1,"h":0.016195524146054185},{"h":0.01744357211289338,"t":"found in the now extinct woolly mammoth.' This repopulation of the tundra and","c":1,"x":0.12962963461672927,"y":0.55087209321013986,"w":0.69341562906901044},{"h":0.015988372380376759,"y":0.56976744171413252,"t":"boreal forests of Eurasia and North America with large mammals could also be a","x":0.13168724427043438,"w":0.71193415323893228,"c":1},{"w":0.72238555908203117,"y":0.5844100821686572,"c":1,"x":0.13160822021526666,"t":"useful factor in reducing carbon emissions - elephants punch holes through snow","h":0.019480582822478332},{"y":0.60239695770186052,"c":1,"t":"and knock down trees, which encourages grass growth. This grass growth would","h":0.018908620863556158,"x":0.13162110065126456,"w":0.71415171305338543},{"w":0.62345677693684887,"h":0.017464116549183006,"c":1,"x":0.13168724929126047,"y":0.62063953472397537,"t":"reduce temperatures, and mitigate emissions from melting permafrost."},{"w":0.63168726603190106,"h":0.016017476296396826,"t":"While the prospect of bringing extinct animals back to life might capture","c":1,"y":0.64534883706251489,"x":0.13168723106028513},{"c":1,"y":0.66279069751492048,"h":0.017441860778592888,"x":0.12962964209193453,"t":"imaginations, it is, of course, far easier to try to save an existing species which","w":0.69547322591145833},{"y":0.68021201413204635,"w":0.70370371500651041,"t":"is merely threatened with extinction. 'Many of the technologies that people have","h":0.014555427856804748,"c":1,"x":0.1316872370390206},{"t":"in mind when they think about de-extinction can be used as a form of \"genetic","y":0.69458154113574044,"h":0.018014325972019019,"w":0.6894053141276042,"x":0.13163181806111537,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"rescue\",' explains Shapiro. She prefers to focus the debate on how this emerging","x":0.1316872351662812,"w":0.71604939778645826,"y":0.71220930217930922,"h":0.016000356213644928},{"t":"technology could be used to fully understand why various species went extinct in","y":0.72965116264387364,"h":0.01598837238037687,"c":1,"w":0.71399175008138027,"x":0.13168725244667256},{"h":0.016026036337772664,"t":"the first place, and therefore how we could use it to make genetic modifications","x":0.13168724614433083,"c":1,"w":0.69958847045898442,"y":0.7470553591522664},{"t":"which could prevent mass extinctions in the future. 'I would also say there's an","x":0.13163362155257802,"y":0.76151870553303502,"w":0.69352711995442706,"h":0.018586494616541049,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"incredible moral hazard to not do anything at all,' she continues. 'We know that","x":0.13168726539773823,"w":0.69753082275390621,"y":0.7790697676599746,"h":0.015988371257085632},{"y":0.79651162774660478,"c":1,"h":0.017441860778592888,"t":"what we are doing today is not enough, and we have to be willing to take some","x":0.13168723800011661,"w":0.69753087361653643},{"y":0.81242638423923952,"w":0.28395060221354163,"x":0.13168725296730319,"h":0.016195524146054185,"t":"calculated and measured risks.'","c":1},{"h":0.013081395583944722,"w":0.024691357612609877,"t":"41","x":0.84773662561756336,"y":0.91715116260773688,"c":1}],"h":3395,"w":2400}